From 9ac79436408d792a1fa65cbf234b6bc4fa6b6413 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Jun 2026 10:52:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] patch 0244 -- #39: robust .pat root_freq unit auto-detect
 (silent-music likely fix)

g2k: GUS music runs (voices commanded) but inaudible; sdl-pg audited their
voice primitives (FC/log-vol/address per DOSBox-X gus.cpp) and they look
correct, pointing at the FREQUENCY mapping (engine).

My note_on already computes playback_hz = sample_rate * note_freq / root_hz
(the playback RATE, ~13kHz for note 60), NOT the bare note frequency -- BUT
that is correct ONLY if root_freq parses to a sane root_hz. The one offline-
unverifiable field is the .pat root_frequency UNIT. The record offset is sound
(modes@55 reads correctly -> the 96-byte layout is anchored -> root_freq@30 is
right), but milliHz-vs-Hz is ambiguous. A wrong unit makes root_hz 1000x off ->
playback_hz ultrasonic or sub-DC -> EVERY note silent (and via the old
g_fp==0->65536 guard, a too-high root_hz degenerated playback_hz to the bare
NOTE frequency -- exactly the silent-voices symptom).

Fix: auto-detect the unit -- pick whichever of root_freq/1000 (milliHz,
canonical) or root_freq (Hz) yields a musically-plausible root pitch
(8..12544 Hz, the MIDI range); fall back to A440 if neither. Cleanly separates
the two (milliHz ~100k+ raw; Hz ~50-2000 raw). Robust to the format ambiguity,
not a blind guess; the GUS_DIAG per-instrument log prints the chosen root_hz +
hz@note60 so the iter shows which unit won (preserves attribution alongside
sdl-pg's vol fix + test-tone).

Built clean; default/non-GUS paths untouched.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp b/src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp
index cac2a0b0..272e8b51 100644
--- a/src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp
+++ b/src/sound/MidiBackendGus.cpp
@@ -332,10 +332,28 @@ bool MidiBackendGus::_upload_pat(const char *base_name, bool is_drum,
   if (loop_start > data_size) loop_start = 0;
 
   // Pitch scaler g_fp = (sample_rate / root_hz) << 16, integer fixed-point.
-  // root_hz = root_freq (milliHz) / 1000. FPU OK here (main-loop). note_on
-  // then does playback_hz = (g_fp * _note_freq[note]) >> 16 with pure ints.
-  double root_hz = (root_freq > 0) ? (root_freq / 1000.0) : 440.0;
-  if (root_hz < 1.0) root_hz = 440.0;
+  // note_on then does playback_hz = (g_fp * _note_freq[note]) >> 16 (pure int).
+  //
+  // patch 0244 (#39 silent-music fix): be ROBUST to the GUS .pat root_frequency
+  // UNIT. The field is canonically milliHz (Hz*1000, e.g. 261626 for C5), so we
+  // divide by 1000 -> root_hz. But some sets/tools store it in Hz directly. If
+  // we guess wrong, root_hz is 1000x off -> playback_hz is 1000x off ->
+  // ultrasonic or sub-DC -> EVERY note silent (the #39 systemic symptom; and
+  // via the old g_fp==0 guard, a too-high root_hz collapsed g_fp to 1.0 so
+  // playback_hz degenerated to the bare NOTE frequency -- exactly sdl-pg's
+  // "note-pitch not playback-rate" hypothesis). Auto-detect: pick whichever
+  // interpretation yields a musically-PLAUSIBLE root pitch (8 Hz .. 12544 Hz,
+  // the full MIDI note range). milliHz data is ~100k+ (the /1000 lands in range,
+  // the raw value is way above 12544); Hz data is ~50-2000 (the raw value lands
+  // in range, /1000 is sub-8). Cleanly separates the two; falls back to A440 if
+  // neither is plausible (corrupt/garbage field). The per-instrument GUS_DIAG
+  // log (below) prints the chosen root_hz so the iter shows which unit won.
+  const double rh_milli = (root_freq > 0) ? (root_freq / 1000.0) : 0.0;
+  const double rh_hz    = (root_freq > 0) ? (double)root_freq    : 0.0;
+  double root_hz;
+  if (rh_milli >= 8.0 && rh_milli <= 12544.0)      root_hz = rh_milli;  // milliHz (canonical)
+  else if (rh_hz >= 8.0 && rh_hz <= 12544.0)       root_hz = rh_hz;     // stored as Hz
+  else                                             root_hz = 440.0;     // implausible -> A440
   const double g = (double)sample_rate / root_hz;
   std::uint32_t g_fp = (std::uint32_t)(g * 65536.0 + 0.5);
   if (g_fp == 0) g_fp = 65536;  // identity guard
